course: dictionary
lesson: 1643
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is right. Context means the words and sentences around the word. «Open supermarket chillers blow a curtain of cold air down the front to keep most of the cold in.» Here a chiller is a machine that keeps food cold, because it is in a supermarket and it blows cold air.
explain: Now read this: «That film was a real chiller, I hid behind the sofa.» Nobody is talking about a fridge. A chiller here is a frightening story or film that gives you a shiver. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: In the UK, people also use chiller informally for a relaxed, calm person or a calm time. Word families help too: chill, chilly and chilling are all linked to the idea of cold, and that link can help you remember the word.
fact: A chiller is a machine or cabinet that keeps food or drink very cold.
fact: A «spine-chiller» is a frightening story or film that gives you a shiver.
fact: In UK informal speech, a chiller can be a relaxed, calm person or time.
fact: Cold slows the growth of germs, which is why chillers help to keep food safe.
fact: Chill, chilly and chilling are related words, all linked to cold.
exercise: «Open supermarket chillers blow a curtain of cold air down the front.» In this sentence, what is a chiller? | *A machine or cabinet that keeps food very cold | A frightening film | A cold drink in a glass | A relaxed, calm person
exercise: Sam says, «That horror book was a proper spine-chiller.» What does spine-chiller mean? | *A frightening story that gives you a shiver | A slow, boring story | A cold spine on a book | A fridge door
exercise: Mum says, «Relax, you're a total chiller.» What might this mean? | *A calm, relaxed person | A person who is always cold | A machine that makes ice | A scary monster
test: «Milk and meat are kept in the chiller at the shop.» What does chiller mean here? | *A machine that keeps food cold | A calm, relaxed person | A type of ice cream | Something that shouts loudly
test: Which word is in the same family as chiller, linked to the idea of cold? | Chore | *Chilly | Chart | Chimp
exam: The word chiller has more than one meaning. What does «That film was a real chiller» most likely mean? | A calm, relaxed person | *A frightening film that gives you a shiver | A slow, dull film | A machine in a shop
